                                                              "summary":  "Josh Brown profiles Ron Baron of Baron Capital, whose Baron Partners Fund has been the top-performing mutual fund in America since 2003, generating over $60 billion in cumulative investor returns. Baron\u0027s edge is rooted in extreme patience and conviction in transformative companies, most notably early and sustained positions in Tesla and SpaceX -- the latter now valued at roughly $25 billion in his portfolio. The piece highlights Baron\u0027s willingness to hold through prolonged criticism and drawdowns that drove away less committed investors. His strategy is built on identifying visionary founders and holding for decades rather than quarters.",
