                                                                                "take":  "Santoli\u0027s narrow-leadership observation is a yellow flag that deserves more weight than it typically gets in bull market narratives. When an index approaches records on the back of 5-10 stocks, the risk is not that those stocks are overvaluedÃƒÆ’Ã‚Â¢ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬Å¡Ã‚Â¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â€šÂ¬Ã‚Âit\u0027s that any company-specific disappointment in that group has an outsized market impact. The constructive read is that light positioning creates fuel for a melt-up; the cautious read is that the market has no shock absorbers if mega-cap earnings disappoint in Q3. The asymmetry here favors holding but hedging tech concentration.",
